@startuml
title Life of an encrypted value
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ActorBorderColor #4A78B5
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  ArrowColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F3F7FD
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
autonumber

actor User
participant Relayer
participant "Coprocessors" as Cop
participant "Gateway" as GW
participant "Contract" as C
participant "InputVerifier" as IV
participant "FHEVMExecutor" as EX
participant "ACL" as ACL
participant "KMS" as KMS

== Encrypt ==
User -> User : encrypt(v, pk) + ZKPoK
User -> Relayer : ciphertext list + proof
Relayer -> GW : register input
GW -> Cop : verification event
Cop -> Cop : verify ZKPoK, store ciphertext,\nderive handles
Cop -> GW : EIP-712 signature over\n(handles, user, contract, chainId)
GW -> Relayer : inputProof = handles + signatures
Relayer -> User : inputProof

== Compute (symbolic on-chain, real off-chain) ==
User -> C : call(handle, inputProof)
C -> IV : FHE.fromExternal
IV -> IV : chainId, version, threshold of\nregistered signers
C -> EX : FHE.add(a, b)
EX -> ACL : isAllowed(a), isAllowed(b)
EX -> EX : handle = hash(op, a, b, ACL,\nchainId, blockhash, timestamp)
EX -> ACL : allowTransient(handle, contract)
EX --> Cop : operation event
C -> ACL : FHE.allow(handle, holder)
ACL --> Cop : Allowed event
Cop -> Cop : evaluate with the evaluation key,\nstore ciphertext under handle
Cop -> GW : ciphertext digest
GW -> GW : majority consensus\n-> material added

== Decrypt ==
User -> Relayer : user decryption(handle, contract,\nephemeral pk, EIP-712 signature)
Relayer -> GW : request
GW -> GW : material added?
GW -> KMS : decrypt request
KMS -> KMS : check ACL replica,\nthreshold decryption,\nre-encrypt under ephemeral pk
KMS -> GW : signed result
GW -> Relayer : re-encrypted plaintext
Relayer -> User : decrypt locally
note over C, KMS #F3F7FD : Public decryption follows the same path, with the oracle\nposting the KMS-signed plaintext back to the contract,\nwhich verifies it through KMSVerifier.
@enduml
